"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[9960],{89960:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"inflyaciya-ssha-sentyabr-2026-toplivo","locale":"en","title":"Expensive fuel pushes US inflation to 3.7% and feeds through to other prices","description":"US inflation rose to 3.7% in September 2026, with core inflation at 2.6%. How expensive fuel spreads into other prices and what Russian data show.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"US consumer prices rose by 3.7% over the year in September 2026, up from 3.4% in August and above analysts\' 3.6% forecast. Prices increased by 0.6% over the month, with gasoline accounting for more than half: it rose by 9.1% in September and 34.2% over the year. Energy overall became 20.4% more expensive year-on-year. But core inflation excluding food and energy also accelerated, to 2.6% from 2.4% in August and above the 2.5% forecast."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"This is how fuel costs spread. A bakery delivers bread to shops in its own van. Diesel becomes more expensive, so the bakery first adds a delivery surcharge to the invoice. A couple of months later, the shop incorporates that surcharge into the loaf\'s price. Next, the cafe buying that bread and the taxi carrying its cook become more expensive. These are second-round effects: a shock to one price spreads into prices not directly connected with it. Expensive oil appears in reports from all 12 districts in the Fed\'s regional Beige Book, and businesses complain about diesel and fuel surcharges throughout the supply chain."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"For the US Federal Reserve, this is a bad sign. Its rate is currently 3.75–4%, following a quarter-point increase in September. Chicago Fed President Austan Goolsbee called the report discouraging: service-sector inflation is above 5% and barely falling. After the report, the probability of an increase on October 27–28 rose from 21.6% to 32.7%. The dollar strengthened against other currencies and US stocks fell, with the S&P 500 down 1.11%."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"Fuel is also rising faster than other prices in Russia, although for different reasons: refinery disruptions and repairs. If that feeds into delivery costs too, other goods will follow. From the start of the year through October 12, gasoline rose by 21.4%, diesel by 13.5% and all consumer prices by 6.1%. Weekly inflation for October 6–12 slowed to 0.11% after a utility-driven 0.96% jump, but food rose by 0.21% and eggs by 2.4%."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"The Bank of Russia expects 2026 inflation of 6–7%. To stay within 7%, prices must rise no more than 0.85% by year-end (1.07 / 1.061). That is about 0.07% a week, whereas the latest week delivered 0.11%. Analysts surveyed by the Bank of Russia expect 7.1%. The regulator will announce a new forecast and rate decision on October 23."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"If fuel\'s second-round effects prove weak, weekly inflation will return to 0.07% or lower, giving the Bank of Russia a reason to consider cutting rates. If delivery, services and food keep becoming more expensive after gasoline, the 14% rate will last longer: credit will stay expensive and deposits will remain attractive."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"Why did US inflation rise in September 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"Gasoline was the main cause: its price rose by 9.1% over the month and 34.2% over the year, contributing more than half of monthly price growth. But core inflation excluding food and energy also accelerated, from 2.4% to 2.6%. Businesses in the Fed survey complain about fuel surcharges across the supply chain, with some also citing import tariffs."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"Will the Fed raise rates because of inflation?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"That has not been decided. After the report, markets estimated a 32.7% probability of an increase at the October 27–28 meeting, versus 21.6% the day before. The current Fed rate is 3.75–4%."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"Will Russian inflation stay within the Bank of Russia\'s 2026 forecast?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"Prices rose by 6.1% from the start of the year through October 12. To keep annual inflation at or below 7%, the top of the Bank of Russia\'s forecast range, prices must increase no more than 0.85% by year-end. Analysts in its survey expect 7.1%; the regulator will provide a new forecast on October 23."}],"sources":[{"label":"Inflation surged in September as U.S. energy costs jumped","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/articles/inflation-surged-september-u-energy-125137111.html"},{"label":"Higher fuel costs lead to price increases, businesses warn the Fed","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/articles/higher-fuel-costs-lead-price-192929072.html"},{"label":"Fed\'s Goolsbee says September CPI \'discouraging\'","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/policy/articles/feds-goolsbee-says-september-cpi-193440276.html"},{"label":"Dollar ticks up, gold slides on US inflation news","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/currencies/articles/dollar-ticks-gold-slides-on-us-inflation-news-193351444.html"},{"label":"Wall Street falls on Wednesday as US inflation accelerates","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1122532"},{"label":"Russian inflation is 0.11% on October 6–12 as annual inflation rises to 7.22%","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1122459"},{"label":"Inflation for October 6–12 is 0.11%","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/economics/news/2026/10/14/1237099-inflyatsiya-sostavila"}],"sourceBodySha256":"28f2c644ef71d7bb0798565c5d39754497c35d4acc2f2fb91243b4680ba43a81"}')}}]);